  "hypothesis": "At least 20 of the 21 frozen articles will satisfy the full rights audit when the JATS-standard NISO ALI license_ref is accepted as an alternative URI pointer, and no untraceable third-party prose will prevent deterministic extraction.",
  "change": "For this separate audit, accept either (1) a descendant XLink href in the exact front/article-meta/permissions/license subtree equal to one of the two Q10-SOURCE-006 CC BY 4.0 URI forms, or (2) a correctly namespaced NISO ALI license_ref element in that subtree whose trimmed text is exactly the canonical HTTPS CC BY 4.0 URI. The ALI namespace must be http://www.niso.org/schemas/ali/1.0/. Require exact XML identity, the frozen OAI canonical HTTPS URI, a consistent article license statement, and no conflicting or unclear terms for abstract/main-body prose. Preserve SOURCE-005/006 unchanged.",
  "conflict_and_body_rights_rule": "Review every license or permission statement in the exact article metadata and rights-relevant notices in body text. An additional license explicitly scoped to data, figures, tables, captions, supplements or media excluded from extraction does not by itself bar abstract/main-body prose; if scope conflicts with or cannot be separated from prose rights, exclude the whole document. Exclude all figures, tables, captions, supplements, media, back matter, references, acknowledgements, permissions and non-prose markup from any eventual text extraction.",
  "control": "Q10-SOURCE-005/006 strict explicit-href screen on the same 21 files (13 permitted hrefs; 8 ALI-only references; zero fully rights-cleared). This is a protocol control, not a data or capability control.",
